// =============================================================================
// Borin Emberhand — Blacksmith / Forge.  Questline: "The Last Ember" (vendor.forge)
// Keystone: the Emberbrand.  Teaches weapon crafting + the Iron economy.
// Stage-aware Talk (the "stemming" mechanic): $q_forge_stage 0→1→2→3→9(bonded).
// Quest verbs (StartQuest/AdvanceQuest/GiveKeystone) come from NPCCommandBridge
// (WO-290); shop/craft/equip from the existing vendor verbs.
// =============================================================================
title: TalkToForge
---
<<if $q_forge_stage == 0>>
    Borin: Hmph. A hero with a starter blade. That iron's soft as cheese — and the good ore's gone bad since the Heart started to dim.
    -> What's wrong with the ore?
        Borin: Aether-rot. Crept in from the west when the Heart dimmed. My forge has been cold a week for want of clean fuel.
    -> Can you forge me something better?
        Borin: Not 'til the forge is lit. Bring me wood and iron and we'll talk about a real weapon.
        <<set $q_forge_stage = 1>>
        <<command: StartQuest vendor.forge>>
        Borin: "The Last Ember," I'm calling it. Get me that fuel.
    -> Just browse your wares.
        <<command: OpenShop "forge">>
<<elseif $q_forge_stage == 1>>
    Borin: Back already? Did you bring the wood and iron to relight the forge?
    -> Here's your fuel.
        <<command: AdvanceQuest vendor.forge>>
        <<set $q_forge_stage = 2>>
        Borin: <i>The forge roars to life.</i> Now THAT'S a sound I've missed. Next: bring me one flawless Aether Crystal to quench the first true blade.
    -> Not yet.
        Borin: Then don't waste my heat. Off with you.
<<elseif $q_forge_stage == 2>>
    Borin: Got that flawless crystal? A blade's only as true as what cools it.
    -> Quench it.
        <<command: AdvanceQuest vendor.forge>>
        <<set $q_forge_stage = 3>>
        Borin: <i>Steam hisses.</i> She's perfect. But steel's only proven in the field — go clear the Stonebelly raid at the west gate, then bring her back to me.
    -> Still hunting one.
        Borin: The flawless ones surface when the veil's thin. Keep your eyes open.
<<elseif $q_forge_stage == 3>>
    Borin: Did the blade hold against the trolls?
    -> The west gate's clear.
        <<command: AdvanceQuest vendor.forge>>
        <<command: GiveKeystone "Emberbrand">>
        <<set $q_forge_stage = 9>>
        Borin: Then it's done — the Emberbrand is yours, and the Last Ember burns again. <i>He lowers his voice.</i> That ore wasn't soured by chance. The rot traces back to the Stone Mountains. Someone's fouling it on purpose.
        Borin: Tell Warden Alric the forge stands ready. And mind the Mountains.
    -> Not yet.
        Borin: Then go earn the blade.
<<else>>
    Borin: The Emberbrand-bearer returns. Forge is hot — what'll it be?
    -> Craft a weapon.
        <<command: OpenCraft "forge">>
    -> Browse the forge wares.
        <<command: OpenShop "forge">>
    -> Upgrade my gear.
        <<command: OpenUpgrade "forge">>
    -> Equip what I have.
        <<command: OpenEquip>>
    -> Nothing today.
        Borin: Then keep that edge sharp.
<<endif>>
===
